{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Completed outcome\n\nMerged commit `586357b70996537ac790a82da56fe6e372d0d3e5` implements a rollback-safe,\ndurable bridge pause/resume surface while preserving old readers, old reconcile vocabulary, and\nexisting workflow/environment behavior.\n\nThe remote `refs/reconciler/gate` blob remains dual-format:\n`gated_mode: \"reconcile-check\"` plus `paused`, `reason`, `who`, and `paused_at`.\nPause provenance uses repository `git user.email` and first-pause UTC RFC3339 time. Same-reason\npause is idempotent and preserves metadata; different reason, blank reason, missing identity,\nmissing remote, and CAS movement refuse without overwrite. Resume deletes only the observed ref\nOID and can recover a corrupt blob without decoding it.\n\nA new pause blocks before pass-lock acquisition or ticket mutation and returns rc 0 with one exact,\nanchored, JSON-decoded `BRIDGE_PAUSED:` line. The scheduled workflow recognizes only that complete\nrc-0 marker and skips commit-and-push. Ordinary rc 0, malformed/unanchored markers, corrupt rc 1,\nand legacy gate rc 4 retain their existing behavior. The pre-gate `reconcile-check` early return\nand old `rebar reconcile --mode` vocabulary remain functional.\n\n## Authoritative evidence\n\n- Gerrit 1549: `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, zero unresolved comments, merged as\n  `586357b709`; retry CI run 31272528686 completed 15/15 jobs successfully.\n- Held-out affected oracle: 82/82 green. Final pre-push affected/module-size oracle: 86/86 green.\n- Static gates: lint, Ruff format, actionlint, complexity, typecheck, config-check, generated CLI\n  reference, module-size, and diff checks green.\n- Mutation teeth: tests went RED when additive `gated_mode` was removed, marker anchoring was\n  weakened, and corrupt-gate traceback handling was regressed; production was restored after each.\n- Primary contract tests:\n  `tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py`,\n  `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_main.py`,\n  `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock_ref_backend.py`,\n  `tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py`, and\n  `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py`.\n- Implementation/docs:\n  `src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py`,\n  `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py`,\n  `_advisory_lock.py`, `__main__.py`,\n  `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`, CLI help/reference, user guide, exit codes, and release\n  notes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Every pause blob retains `gated_mode: reconcile-check` and carries `paused`, `reason`,\n      `who`, and `paused_at`; the vendored pre-change decoder accepts it, legacy mutating modes\n      remain blocked, and `reconcile-check` keeps its pre-gate early return.\n- [x] `who` is repository `git user.email`; missing identity refuses without writing;\n      `paused_at` is first-pause UTC RFC3339; blank/different reasons refuse and same-reason pause\n      preserves both metadata fields.\n- [x] `rebar bridge pause REASON` and `resume` are additive write paths over expected-old-OID\n      CAS; missing remote and conflicts fail with current state and no blind retry/overwrite;\n      absent resume succeeds; corrupt resume clears the observed ref without decoding.\n- [x] A genuine pause exits 0 before lock/pass/ticket mutation with the exact single-line,\n      four-key `BRIDGE_PAUSED` JSON contract; the workflow accepts only a complete anchored rc-0\n      marker and skips commit-and-push.\n- [x] A corrupt remote gate exits 1 with the exact recovery line, no traceback, and no lock/ticket\n      mutation; following the instruction with `bridge resume` clears it and exits 0.\n- [x] Existing legacy gated-mode exit behavior, ordinary success, benign mappings, generic errors,\n      old reconcile vocabulary, and scheduled workflow behavior remain functional and covered.\n- [x] Help, generated reference, user guide, exit-code docs, and release notes expose the staged\n      `preview/sync/pause/resume` surface; no `--until`, expiry, new-only blob, gate rename, or\n      old-vocabulary removal shipped.\n\n## Residual disposition\n\nMCP and library pause/resume parity is filed in existing dependent story\n`f789-3f9d-8b35-4e0d`. Near-cap `_ref_lock.py` restructuring remains owned by\n`5e53-234f-5c65-477d` and is linked to this story. No test exclusion or weaker validation remains.\n"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786216614529740001,"uuid":"661eaf9e-9945-42d6-afbd-08b2efdc44e5"}